1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,679
The devices to quote.

2
00:00:01,679 --> 00:00:08,125
Situational irony: she dislikes the man she has never met and is drawn to the man who ignores her.

3
00:00:08,125 --> 00:00:09,830
Free indirect style.

4
00:00:09,830 --> 00:00:11,979
The antithesis on the bench.

5
00:00:11,979 --> 00:00:13,372
Allusion to Whitman.

6
00:00:13,372 --> 00:00:16,875
Euphemism: she calls her desire only a folly.

7
00:00:16,875 --> 00:00:21,067
Foreshadowing: I should like him better if he did give me trouble.

8
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:22,369
And the open ending.

